  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250). The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the transformer+weighted advantage is specific to imagenet_vit_l or generalizable. Config_047 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) is the only untested configuration that isolates the image encoder variable while holding the best aggregation and fusion fixed. It completes the critical 2x2 comparison for the top-performing architecture family. Even though resnet50 has underperformed vit_l in prior tests (0.6878 vs 0.7207 with concat), testing it with the stronger weighted fusion may reveal whether the gap narrows. This is the best use of the penultimate experiment because it either confirms imagenet_vit_l is essential (guiding the final experiment toward other untested dimensions) or reveals a competitive alternative, reducing uncertainty before the last experiment."
